# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  CROWN PIERCE PORTFOLIO — ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
#  USAGE:
#  1) LOCAL DEVELOPMENT
#     Copy this file to  .env.local  (gitignored) and fill in the values:
#         cp .env.example .env.local
#  2) NETLIFY (production)
#     Paste the KEY=VALUE lines below into:
#         Netlify → Site configuration → Environment variables
#     (Use the "Import from .env" / bulk paste option to add them all at once.)
#
#  NOTE: Netlify treats every env var as a potential secret and scans build
#  output for their values. The two SECRETS_SCAN_* vars below teach the
#  scanner which paths/keys to ignore so the build isn't blocked.

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  AI CHAT ASSISTANT — Google Gemini  (the chat widget in the corner)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# REQUIRED for live AI answers. Without it the chatbot gracefully falls
# back to a local offline knowledge base.
# Get a free key at:  https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# OPTIONAL — the Gemini model to use.
# If unset, the app defaults to "gemini-3.6-flash" (see app/api/chat/route.ts).
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.6-flash

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  NETLIFY SECRETS SCANNING  (Netlify-only, harmless locally)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Skip the scanner over Next.js/Turbopack build-cache files. Your API key's
# value is cached there during every build, but those files are never
# deployed — so excluding them is safe and prevents false positives.
SECRETS_SCAN_OMIT_PATHS=**/.next/cache/**

# Don't flag GEMINI_MODEL as a secret — it's a model name that legitimately
# appears in source code as the default value.
SECRETS_SCAN_OMIT_KEYS=GEMINI_MODEL
